    "Search (searchPage) and the destination router (routeKey) both read the canonical word, so every word of a concept gives the identical results and the identical landing.",
    "Edit this file; no code change is needed (netlify/functions/_search-core.js conceptTokens reads it).",
    "canonical: the word the catalogue's own titles use (they are mostly English). It must not be a word of another concept.",
    "words: the other words for it. Write them in plain lower case; accents, case and punctuation are ignored ('muñeca' = 'muneca').",
    "  A phrase of several words is matched before single words, longest first ('lentes de sol' before 'lentes').",
    "  Plurals are by rule (-s, -es), and so is a one-letter typo of a word of 5+ letters (two from 10 letters) that the catalogue does not carry: do not list them.",
    "A concept whose canonical is a phrase with no other words is a GUARD: it keeps that phrase as typed ('polo shirt' is not 'polo').",
    "Never rewritten: a word inside a store's or brand's name ('Polo Ralph Lauren', 'Alien Workshop'); a word the query's own brand writes as its line name ('Guess Marciano').",
    "scripts/test/search-variants-tests.mjs routes every word of every concept, with a plural, an accent and a typo, and requires one identical destination."
